cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vina-Ion-Metal, please cite it, its predecessor VinaMetal, and the AutoDock Vina / AutoDock 4 foundations listed in the references."
title: Vina-Ion-Metal
type: software
version: 1.0.2
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cristhianyaranganana-arch/Vina-Ion-Metal"
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - metalloprotein
  - metal coordination
  - AutoDock Vina
  - C++
authors:
  - name: "Christian Yaranga Nana"
    email: cristhianyaranganana@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5539-0526"
    affiliation: "Universidad Norbert Wiener"
abstract: >-
  Vina-Ion-Metal is a fork of AutoDock Vina 1.2.7 that integrates AutoDock 4
  metal coordination physics into the native scoring function: metal-specific
  12-6 van der Waals terms, a differentiable coordination-number penalty with
  lenient/strict regimes and a bounded geometry bonus, all with analytic
  gradients. It detects the coordination sites already occupied by the rigid
  receptor (with typing-independent geometric diagnostics) and adjusts the
  ligand coordination-number target automatically, and ships a robust
  receptor-preparation pipeline that types Cu2+/Ni2+ ions which Meeko cannot
  emit. It is the corrected successor of VinaMetal 1.0.0, fixing the 16
  problems identified by the 2026 technical audit. The tool is designed as a
  mechanistic pose filter for metalloenzyme docking, not as an affinity
  predictor; its metal scoring weights are provisional heuristics pending a
  calibration benchmark.
